# Copy to  tools\.discord-webhook  and replace the line below. That file is gitignored.
#
# The fallback announcement route, used only when no bot token is configured. A webhook
# posts to exactly one channel and cannot read anything, which makes it the safer option
# if all you want is release notes going out.
#
# The URL is itself the credential - anyone holding it can post to that channel as the
# webhook. Treat it like a password. It can be deleted and recreated from the channel's
# Integrations settings at any time.
#
# Channel settings -> Integrations -> Webhooks -> New Webhook -> Copy Webhook URL.
# The whole URL goes on one line, nothing else in the file.

https://discord.com/api/webhooks/PUT_THE_WEBHOOK_URL_HERE
